**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** The constructor suite's sample, source and Library facts read the shipped catalogue instead of the code seeds (001 §B 'tests load the same files'; the S1.7 brief: re-point every test that reads a seed value to the BuiltinCatalogue fixture, numbers unchanged). Files, all in `OpticalConstructor.Tests/`: `SampleProxyTests.fs`, `PropagationTests.fs`, `ExperimentProxyTests.fs`, `ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.fs`, `ExperimentRunTests.fs`, `PlacedSampleEmissionTests.fs`, `LibraryProxyTests.fs`, `SourceLibraryTests.fs`, `PolarizerBehaviorTests.fs`. Re-point rules (S1.7; the same in every re-point step). `builtInEntries` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.materials ()`; `standardCategories` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.categories ()`; `MaterialLibrary.standard` (written `standard` under `open MaterialLibrary`) becomes `{ entries = BuiltinCatalogue.materials () }`; `SeedSamples.allSeedSamples` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.samples ()`; `SeedSamples.<name>` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.sample SampleIds.<name>Id` and `SeedSamples.<name>.id` becomes `SampleIds.<name>Id` (step 15's names); `SeedSources.allSeedSources` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.sources ()`; `SeedSources.reference600` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.source PresetIds.source600`; the `SeedSources.tunables` list becomes `[ PresetIds.xenonMonochromator; PresetIds.tiSapphireTunable; PresetIds.supercontinuum; PresetIds.euvBeamline ] |> List.map BuiltinCatalogue.source`, and one tunable source becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.source PresetIds.xenonMonochromator`; `seedEntries` becomes `(BuiltinCatalogue.samples () |> List.map SampleItem) @ BuiltinCatalogue.presets ()`; `Library.createInMemory ()` (written `createInMemory ()` under `open Library`) becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.library ()`; and the self-seeding stores become the fixture's doubles with the same arguments (step 45): `MaterialProxy.createInMemory r v` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.materialStore r v`, `SampleProxy.createInMemory v` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.sampleStore v` and `CategoryProxy.createInMemory r` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.categoryStore r`. A fact that took a seed by its list position (`List.head`, `List.item`) takes the same entry by its well-known id (`MaterialIds`, `CategoryIds`, `SampleIds`, `PresetIds`), so it still tests the entry it tested; a fact that compared ordered lists built from the seed lists builds both sides from the fixture, and compares order-independently only where the product's order is not the fixture's row order (the S1.3 step 20 precedent). Every fact keeps its name and its assertions, every count and every number stays. A comment or doc, an `open`'s trailing comment included, that names a seed or a self-seeding store names the fixture member instead, in no more words, and an `open` nothing needs any more goes. No product file, fixture member or fact is added. Per file: `LibraryProxyTests`' module proxy is `BuiltinCatalogue.library ()`, and its fact `libraryTrees returns at least one tree and every leaf entry id resolves` now runs over the derived tree (step 47) with its assertions unchanged; `SourceLibraryTests` builds every Library through `BuiltinCatalogue.library ()` and `sampleStore`, its unqualified `createInMemory ()` included, so it calls no `createInMemory` but `SourceProxy.createInMemory`; `the seeded tree lists every seeded source under Sources` collects the `Sources` group's leaves recursively, as its `leaves` already does, and compares them with the ids of `BuiltinCatalogue.sources ()` order-independently, because the derived tree lists fixed lines before tunable sources; `PlacedSampleEmissionTests`' library is `BuiltinCatalogue.library ()` and its three ids are the `toElementValueId` of `SampleIds.euvMoSiId`, `glassFilm600Id` and `glassPlate1mmId`; `ExperimentRunTests` checks the four tunable `PresetIds` sources of the rules; `PropagationTests` builds its material store through `materialStore` and resolves `BuiltinCatalogue.samples ()`.

**Acceptance.** After the re-point, `git grep -n -E "SeedSamples|SeedSources|seedEntries|seedTrees|builtInEntries|standardCategories|seedExperiments|(MaterialProxy|SampleProxy|CategoryProxy).createInMemory |Library.createInMemory " -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PropagationTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentRunTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PlacedSampleEmissionTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryProxyTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SourceLibraryTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PolarizerBehaviorTests.fs MUST find nothing, and `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SourceLibraryTests.fs` MUST NOT contain `(createInMemory ())`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass with its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the seven s07 invariants MUST pass.
